{"id":"y7-flowcharts-l4","label":"7CT.01 L4: Sub-routines","steps":[{"id":"do-now","label":"Do Now: Recap Selection","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l4-do-now","validatorKey":"y7l4_do_now","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Recap Selection</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A quick recap before today's new idea.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-code\"><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">1&nbsp;&nbsp;INPUT Score</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">2&nbsp;&nbsp;IF Score &gt;= 60 THEN</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Pass\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">4&nbsp;&nbsp;ELSE</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;OUTPUT \"Fail\"</div><div class=\"lesson-code-line\">6&nbsp;&nbsp;ENDIF</div></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><h3>The user enters 40</h3><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-do-now-a\">(a) State whether Score &gt;= 60 is true or false. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-do-now-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-do-now-b\">(b) State which line runs, line 3 or line 5. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-do-now-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-do-now-c\">(c) State the output. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-do-now-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-c\" aria-label=\"Do Now part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l4-do-now-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l4-do-now-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"title","label":"Sub-routines","content":"<div class=\"lesson-title-slide\"><p class=\"lesson-title-kicker\">Computational Thinking</p><h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Sub-routines</h2><p>Year 7, 7CT.01 L4</p></div>"},{"id":"why-subroutines","label":"Why Reuse Part of an Algorithm?","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Why Reuse Part of an Algorithm?</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Some sets of instructions are needed more than once in the same program.</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>A sub-routine is a named, reusable part of an algorithm.</li><li>It is written once, as its own separate flowchart.</li><li>CALL jumps execution into the sub-routine from anywhere in the main flowchart.</li><li>Writing it once and calling it avoids typing, and fixing, the same steps more than once.</li></ul>"},{"id":"commands","label":"The CALL Block","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7l4-commands-stepper","stepperKey":"y7l4_call_commands","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">The CALL Block</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">One new shape, and a new way instructions can jump between two flowcharts.</p><div id=\"y7l4-commands-stepper\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"worked-trace","label":"Trace the Call","type":"stepper","stepperId":"y7l4-trace-stepper","stepperKey":"y7l4_trace_the_call","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Trace the Call</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Follow Main step by step. When it CALLs DrawSquare, follow DrawSquare's own flowchart until it ends, then come back to Main.</p><div id=\"y7l4-trace-stepper\" class=\"lesson-stepper\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-1","label":"Match the Effect","type":"click-match","containerId":"y7l4-match","items":[{"id":"call-once","left":"Start, CALL DrawSquare, End","right":"One square is drawn"},{"id":"call-twice-turn","left":"Start, CALL DrawSquare, Turn right 90, CALL DrawSquare, End","right":"Two squares, rotated 90 degrees apart"},{"id":"call-twice-no-turn","left":"Start, CALL DrawSquare, CALL DrawSquare, End","right":"Two squares, drawn in exactly the same place"},{"id":"no-call","left":"Start, End","right":"Nothing is drawn"}],"content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Match the Effect</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Click a Main sequence on the left, then click what it draws on the right.</p><div class=\"icontrol-match\" id=\"y7l4-match\"><svg class=\"icontrol-match-svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><defs><marker id=\"icontrol-arrow\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"4\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z\"></path></marker></defs></svg><div class=\"icontrol-match-col click-match-left\"></div><div class=\"icontrol-match-col click-match-right\"></div></div><div class=\"icontrol-match-status\" id=\"y7l4-match-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>"},{"id":"activity-2","label":"Predict the Outcome","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l4-activity-2","validatorKey":"y7l4_activity_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Predict the Outcome</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A new sub-routine you have not seen traced yet.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Sub-routine: Beep</h3><p>Start &rarr; Say \"Beep\" &rarr; Wait 1 second &rarr; Say \"Boop\" &rarr; End</p></div><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><h3>Main</h3><p>Start &rarr; CALL Beep &rarr; CALL Beep &rarr; End</p></div></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-activity-2-a\">(a) State how many times \"Beep\" is said in total. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-activity-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-2-a\" aria-label=\"Activity 2 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-activity-2-b\">(b) State the very last thing said. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-activity-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-2-b\" aria-label=\"Activity 2 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-activity-2-c\">(c) State how many times Beep is written out in full. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-activity-2-c\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"activity-2-c\" aria-label=\"Activity 2 part c\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l4-activity-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 3 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l4-activity-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div>"},{"id":"formative","label":"Check Your Understanding","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Check Your Understanding</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Questions to ask around the room:</p><ul class=\"lesson-facts\"><li>What does CALL do?</li><li>Where does control go after a sub-routine's End?</li><li>Can the same sub-routine be called more than once?</li><li>What is written only once but can run many times?</li><li>If Main has two CALLs to the same sub-routine, how many times does the sub-routine itself need to be written?</li></ul>"},{"id":"plenary","label":"Plenary: Find the Error","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l4-plenary","validatorKey":"y7l4_plenary","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: Find the Error</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A sub-routine called Blink should turn a light on, wait, then turn it off. It is written as:</p><div class=\"lesson-flow-task\"><p>1 Start &rarr; 2 Light on &rarr; 3 Light on &rarr; 4 Wait &rarr; 5 End</p></div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-plenary-a\">(a) State the number of the step that is wrong. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-plenary-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-plenary-b\">(b) State what that step should say instead. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-plenary-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l4-plenary-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l4-plenary-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"},{"id":"plenary-2","label":"Plenary: After the Call","type":"short-answer-validation","validatorId":"y7l4-plenary-2","validatorKey":"y7l4_plenary_2","content":"<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Plenary: After the Call</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">A sub-routine called Flash is: Start &rarr; Light on &rarr; Light off &rarr; End. Main is: Start &rarr; CALL Flash &rarr; Say \"Done\" &rarr; End.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-plenary-2-a\">(a) State the very next instruction that runs after Flash's End. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-plenary-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-a\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y7l4-plenary-2-b\">(b) State whether execution returns to Main's own Start after Flash finishes. [1]</label><input id=\"y7l4-plenary-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"plenary-2-b\" aria-label=\"Plenary 2 part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y7l4-plenary-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y7l4-plenary-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"}],"validators":{"y7l4_do_now":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*false\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"When the user enters 40, is 40 >= 60 true or false?"},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(line\\s*)?5\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The condition is false, so the ELSE branch runs."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*fail\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Line 5 outputs \"Fail\"."}],"y7l4_activity_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*2\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Beep runs from start to finish twice, so \"Beep\" is said twice in total."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*boop\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"The second CALL to Beep finishes with Say \"Boop\", the very last thing said."},{"suffix":"c","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*(once|1)\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Beep is written once. CALLing it twice does not mean writing it twice."}],"y7l4_plenary":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*3\\s*$","flags":""},"feedback":"Compare each step with what Blink should do: on, wait, off."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"light.*off|off","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Step 3 should turn the light off, not on again."}],"y7l4_plenary_2":[{"suffix":"a","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"say.*done|done","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Flash finishes, so control returns to Main, directly after the CALL."},{"suffix":"b","pattern":{"__regex":true,"source":"^\\s*no\\s*$","flags":"i"},"feedback":"Control never returns to Main's own Start, only to the line straight after the CALL."}]},"pseudocodeValidators":{}}